WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.741
Type errors barely

00:00:01.553 --> 00:00:02.802
slow coding agents

00:00:02.614 --> 00:00:03.239
down

00:00:03.774 --> 00:00:05.141
Evil Martians tested

00:00:04.953 --> 00:00:05.755
the claim that

00:00:05.566 --> 00:00:06.828
static types make

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.889
coding agents better

00:00:08.055 --> 00:00:09.457
across ten languages

00:00:09.269 --> 00:00:10.248
and hundreds of

00:00:10.095 --> 00:00:11.073
agent runs

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:12.710
Typed and dynamic

00:00:12.522 --> 00:00:13.783
languages tied at

00:00:13.595 --> 00:00:15.540
about 65 percent solved

00:00:15.623 --> 00:00:17.108
and TypeScript never

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.181
beat plain JavaScript

00:00:17.993 --> 00:00:19.066
in three public

00:00:18.878 --> 00:00:19.762
benchmarks

00:00:20.294 --> 00:00:21.614
Fixing type errors

00:00:21.426 --> 00:00:22.334
took under one

00:00:22.145 --> 00:00:23.230
percent of agent

00:00:23.042 --> 00:00:23.560
time

00:00:23.773 --> 00:00:24.834
while reading code

00:00:24.645 --> 00:00:25.553
was the biggest

00:00:25.365 --> 00:00:26.013
cost

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:28.088
up to 41 minutes per run

00:00:28.614 --> 00:00:29.628
Full story on

00:00:29.439 --> 00:00:30.335
the dashboard
